/Title (As electricity demand continues to grow, peak demand periods place significant stress on the power grid. During these hours, electricity consumption can approach or exceed available supply, causing transmission lines, transformers, and substations to operate near their limits. If this stress is not managed effectively, equipment may overheat, relays would trip, and localized failures can cascade across the network, potentially resulting in large-scale blackouts.)
